title: Suspicious eBPF Program Load
id: 5b362014-536f-40c3-9beb-df0529683dc4
status: experimental
description: Detects loading of eBPF programs via bpftool or unusual bpf() usage from non-observability processes, a technique modern Linux rootkits use to hide processes, files, and network connections in kernel space.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1014/
logsource:
  product: linux
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    Image|endswith: '/bpftool'
    CommandLine|contains:
      - 'prog load'
      - 'prog attach'
  selection_alt:
    CommandLine|contains:
      - 'bpf_probe_write'
      - 'BPF_PROG_TYPE_KPROBE'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - CommandLine
  - User
  - Image
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate observability tooling (Cilium, Falco)
level: high
tags:
  - attack.defense_evasion
  - attack.t1014
